     "explanation": "A heavier object does feel a stronger gravitational pull (bigger m_grav), but it is also proportionally harder to accelerate (bigger m_inert). Because these two masses are exactly equal, the ratio m_grav / m_inert equals 1 and cancels out of the equation, leaving a = g for every object. The heavier pull and the greater resistance perfectly balance, which is exactly what Galileo observed.",
