     "explanation": "The effects push opposite ways and you **subtract** them: -7 (speed slows the clock) + 45 (weaker gravity speeds it up) = **+38 microseconds/day fast**, dominated by the **general-relativistic** gravity term. Left uncorrected, that clock error grows into roughly 10 km of position error per day (38 us x 300 m/us), so engineers detune the clocks before launch to compensate.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">ADDING UP THE TWO EFFECTS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">They pull in opposite directions</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"190\" width=\"800\" height=\"150\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">SPECIAL RELATIVITY (speed)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">clock runs SLOW</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"322\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">- 7 us/day</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"380\" width=\"800\" height=\"150\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">GENERAL RELATIVITY (gravity)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"478\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">clock runs FAST</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"512\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">+ 45 us/day</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"580\" x2=\"900\" y2=\"580\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"620\" width=\"800\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"675\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">NET = + 38 us/day FAST</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">Gravity wins — general relativity dominates</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"768\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\">-7 + 45 = +38</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"840\" width=\"800\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"895\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">UNCORRECTED CONSEQUENCE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">38 us x 300 m/us = about 10 km drift per day</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\">So the clocks are detuned before launch</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Subtract the two effects: +38 microseconds/day, dominated by gravity"
     }
