     "explanation": "Hubble's law, v = H0 times d, makes recession speed directly proportional to distance. Triple the distance d and you triple the speed v, since the Hubble constant H0 is the same everywhere. This is exactly what the stretching-space picture demands: more space between you and a galaxy means more dough to stretch, so it drifts away faster. It also confirms the galaxies are not flying through space, but being carried by space that is itself expanding.",
